{"title":"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Analysis)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Analysis)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Recursive_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Recursive Approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Solution_2_Done_Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Solution 2 Done Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(If_you_don&#39;t_notice_anything)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (If you don't notice anything)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Inversions_of_Permutations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Inversions of Permutations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Just_Math⚡\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Just Math⚡</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the minimum number of successive swaps of adjacent letters in the string <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> that are needed to change the string to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/0/1f0181dacee440ec414579fe73a564d2307c75e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEDCBA?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" /> (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swaps are required to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/747eb612b95cb550f5b0cf380e465fb41dafc300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBA;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> one such sequence of swaps is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e091fc91dcdf30f76a71c0b343521b66a435b85c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC\\to BAC\\to BCA\\to CBA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"262\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/4899db3d1e73a119ba4f107f7c510246a73ef518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~10\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~12\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~15\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Analysis.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Analysis)\">Solution 1 (Analysis)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Analysis)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Procedurally, it takes:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swaps for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to move to the sixth spot, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/3/2b33839deccddb3fd1c98fde85c431ec69b89c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDEFA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swaps for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to move to the fifth spot, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a5496a48ce0ab9066a6d6996c68eddf5f63acd59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDEFBA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swaps for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to move to the fourth spot, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/31985dc63b7421fddbe15808612fc10870bcd29a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFCBA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swaps for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to move to the third spot, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdb71e8a433d0c886e45b257a1a34568e3c6eecf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EFDCBA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> swap for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to move to the second spot (so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> becomes the first spot), giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7deac8c779b721ba85a05af69b32f7b4d1ffefe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEDCBA.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Together, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22fce673653b920050827f9792949f4a8418c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+4+3+2+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"230\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Recursive_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Recursive_Approach)\">Solution 2 (Recursive Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Recursive Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can proceed by a recursive tactic on the number of letters in the string.\n</p><p>Looking at the string <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> moves needed to change it to the string <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Then, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> move to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> moves needed for three letters (said in the problem).\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> moves needed to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e4610cce360b18ee1b0918866cbb80d93e831acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We see a pattern of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190c4e05344caaa4af9fb9d253f951d0d9cad2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1,3,6,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />. We notice that the difference between consecutive terms is increasing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so in the same way, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> letters, we would need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> moves, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we would need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718a7f9bcf263fad1c9033915be35db685041926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> moves.\n</p><p>Thinking why, when we start making these moves, we see that for a string of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> moves to move the last letter to the front. After, we get a string that will be changed identically to a string of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. This works in our pattern above and is another way to think about the problem!\n</p><p>~world123\n</p><p>Note: \n</p><p>The sequence consists of triangular numbers shifted a term up (as it starts with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.)\nThus, our explicit formula is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558ddcb719a0d41a0252fc3516330de5dd17a789.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{(n-1)(n+1-1)}{2} = \\dfrac{(n)(n-1)}{2}\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"38\" /> and as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> in this case (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> letters), our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/2897404c74bb196b93dc1af953846468ab017297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{(6)(6-1)}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"172\" height=\"40\" /> \n</p><p>~NSAoPS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Solution_2_Done_Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Solution_2_Done_Fast)\">Solution 3 (Solution 2 Done Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Solution 2 Done Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that the most efficient way to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5667d4d889deae2d5809824190b35cd6dc475c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEDCBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> is the same as changing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a399e34c1a3a7064a9a3a80a23b56a0551cff68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EDCBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> and then moving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the front in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> moves. Similarly, this would carry on downwards, where to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a399e34c1a3a7064a9a3a80a23b56a0551cff68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EDCBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> would be to change <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e4610cce360b18ee1b0918866cbb80d93e831acc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and move <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times to the front. This pattern will carry on until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756c98caf7386de206b9f9b640c43c12124d4ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0(A)+1(B)+2(C)+3(D)+4(E)+5(F)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"339\" height=\"20\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718a7f9bcf263fad1c9033915be35db685041926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> moves.\n</p><p>~Moonwatcher22\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28If_you_don.27t_notice_anything.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(If_you_don't_notice_anything)\">Solution 4 (If you don't notice anything)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (If you don&#39;t notice anything)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Simply, just blindly doing it, the most straightforward way is to shift F all the way back. From ABCDEF:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f97c69f0ea1eba7ce40c2c8c97008d67a65295d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDFE -&gt;ABCFDE -&gt;ABFCDE -&gt;AFBCDE -&gt;FABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"590\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For E:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e133d21d6d9561bed8ba4ea7adda1d4fc8728ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FABCED -&gt; FABECD -&gt; FAEBCD -&gt; FEABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"464\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For D:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/2826ea8ab4a86386597271a12f202e130ddbc9f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEABDC -&gt; FEADBC -&gt; FEDABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"339\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For C:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143f4beaacd3ca3c29f7ee048aa18f59543c9274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEDACB -&gt; FEDCAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For B:\n</p><p>FEDCBA\n</p><p>That's it, you don't need to do it with A. Still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718a7f9bcf263fad1c9033915be35db685041926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> moves.\n</p><p>~pepper2831\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Inversions_of_Permutations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Inversions_of_Permutations)\">Solution 5 (Inversions of Permutations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Inversions of Permutations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the letters <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0e530ca11be5fa91e36be4b2e22182215ca2a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D, E, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"16\" /> correspond to the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/daed80beb504ec2c25c905a2232ee8f460e060e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. We want to find the number of swaps required to transform the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5ba3c0c313b074354799e233de0065f3a9bb66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 2 3 4 5 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> into the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a2568fda50856526cfff8c4da5e780eacecd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 5 4 3 2 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Here, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/b/b5ba3c0c313b074354799e233de0065f3a9bb66c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 2 3 4 5 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> be the natural order. Then the total number of inversions of the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a2568fda50856526cfff8c4da5e780eacecd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 5 4 3 2 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b165eab59ec499f271177f5eaf423f4603a3562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+5=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"176\" height=\"14\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718a7f9bcf263fad1c9033915be35db685041926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~tsun26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3E881mgzXO8\">https://youtu.be/3E881mgzXO8</a>\n</p><p>~mr_mathman\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I\">https://youtu.be/l3VrUsZkv8I</a>\n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Pi_Academy\">Video Solution by Pi Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Pi Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6qYaJsgqkbs?si=K2Ebwqg-Ro8Yqoiv\">https://youtu.be/6qYaJsgqkbs?si=K2Ebwqg-Ro8Yqoiv</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution 1 by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j-37jvqzhrg?si=ieBRx0-CUihcKttE&amp;t=616\">https://youtu.be/j-37jvqzhrg?si=ieBRx0-CUihcKttE&amp;t=616</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-EFTk2pBFug\">https://youtu.be/-EFTk2pBFug</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_o5zagJVe1U\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_o5zagJVe1U</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Just_Math.E2.9A.A1\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Just_Math⚡\">Video Solution by Just Math⚡</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Just Math⚡\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KrkjGpk1uZs\">https://youtu.be/KrkjGpk1uZs</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Dr. David\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/aeckUgolmIM\">https://youtu.be/aeckUgolmIM</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=890s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4b_YLnyegtw&amp;t=890s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A\">2024 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 10B Problems\">2023 AMC 10B Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 10B Problems\">2024 AMC 10B Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10A_